# Everything is stored and checked out with LF, on every operating system.
#
# A machine clones this repository to /srv/ansiwise-catalog and reads it with Linux tools. A file
# that arrived with CRLF carries a carriage return at the end of every line there: a shell script
# rendered out of a template fails with "bad interpreter", a systemd unit takes the carriage return
# into the value of every setting, and a YAML block scalar writes it into whatever it produces.
# Git applies the LAST matching pattern - keep any exception below this line.
* text=auto eol=lf

# The two kinds this repository is made of, said out loud so that a file whose bytes git reads as
# binary is still stored and checked out as text.
*.yaml text eol=lf
*.tpl  text eol=lf
